Z||000000||danny boy||01-28-2001||06:14 PM|||| I finally went to get my GT from Eds.While not everything went as smooth as I would have liked, I made it in one piece.<BR> Just as I crossed the Alabama state line, a white 5.0 mustang pulled up beside me(I was in my stealth),looked over and smiled,then took off. I couldnt resist....<BR> I was about 3 miles from Ed when I went to stop at a lite and CRUNCH CRUNCH KABANG! something in the drive line broke.I made is to Eds and it quit. I walked in and Ed informed me that he lost mt spoiler.He gave me another one which is in awful shape,but what could I do?I sold my wheels to a kid that worked there and he never paid me for them so I took another set down. when I got there one had a flat tire so I ended up buying another set from Ed.I'm home now and for the first time in 1yr my car is back in my garage.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-28-2001||06:19 PM||||Geez, I'm sorry about the bad luck.  I would be afraid to go out of the house if I had that bad of a day, might get hit by some crazy senile old lady driver or something...<P>Hope your day brightens up.||||reg||1
